@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
actor Player
participant MovementGame as Game
participant GridWorld as World
participant "SpellEffects / SummonRules" as Effects
participant GameSession as Session
participant MenuPanel as Menu
Player -> Game : Commit action
Game -> World : Move / wait / melee / cast boundary
loop Effects in stable order while attempt active
  World -> Effects : Resolve one damage effect
  Effects -> World : Apply health changes; check_terminal()
  alt Stalker killed in this effect
    World -> World : Latch COMPLETED (even if player also died)
  else Player killed without stalker death
    World -> World : Latch PLAYER_DIED
  else No terminal result
    World -> World : Continue next effect / actor / stage
  end
end
note over World, Effects
Terminal state cancels melee and cast continuations.
No later damage, retaliation, regeneration or arrival runs.
A committed player effect consumes its boundary once.
end note
World --> Game : Terminal outcome
alt COMPLETED
  Game -> Game : Clear queued input / selectors; hide gameplay controls
  Game -> Menu : open_completion()
  Menu --> Player : Thanks for playing / Load / Main Menu
  note right of Menu
  Escape cannot resume.
  Load uses existing slots; Back returns here.
  Successful load adopts an earlier playable world.
  end note
else PLAYER_DIED
  Game -> Session : restart_after_death()
  Session -> World : discard()
  Session -> Game : world_changed (fresh Loop)
end
note over Session, World
The first terminal result is latched.
A later callback cannot change death into victory,
repeat a reset, or resume an abandoned world.
end note
@enduml
